    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d364">

                <pb facs="0425" n="419" xml:id="pg419"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/20316: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Second Secretary of Embassy in the Soviet Union</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Thompson</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-03-15T13:00:00+03:00">March 15, 1942—1
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received March 16—2 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>71. My 68, March 12, 3 p.m.<anchor n="40" xml:id="d364-f1"/> Garreau<anchor
                        n="41" xml:id="d364-f2"/> informed me yesterday that Molotov had sent for
                    him and had received him with great cordiality. He told him that so far as the
                    Soviet Union is concerned, de Gaulle<anchor n="42" xml:id="d364-f3"/> is the
                    true representative of the French people and that Russia desires the restoration
                    of a strong France. He said that Molotov agreed in principle to a French
                    division being sent to the Russian front provided the British were willing to
                    release them. Garreau informed me that the matter has already been discussed
                    with the British and that de Gaulle contemplates sending his best Syrian
                    division.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Kuibyshev.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Thompson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d364-f1" n="40" xml:id="d364-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d364-f2" n="41" xml:id="d364-f2-content">
                <p>Roger Garreau, delegate of the French National Committee with personal rank of
                    Minister; he had arrived in Moscow on March 8, 1942.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d364-f3" n="42" xml:id="d364-f3-content">
                <p>Gen. Charles de Gaulle, president of the French National Committee, leader of the
                    Free French.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
